<title>USA: American Telecasting stake cut by Tarian.</title>
<headline>American Telecasting stake cut by Tarian.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tarian Properties Inc said Tuesday it cut its stake in American Telecasting Inc to 1,225,000 Class A common shares or 4.95 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the company, based in Ireland, said it sold 895,000 Class A common shares between January 17 and January 27 at prices ranging from $2.8125 and $3.25 per share.</p>
<p>American Telecasting, based in Colorado Springs, Co., operates wireless cable television systems.</p>
